{
  "_": "きせかえ. Read by the shop AND by the server, so a price is a price and a level is a level. The page draws what this file says and the room charges what this file says; neither has its own copy. Colours are hex strings because a JSON file full of seven-digit decimals is a JSON file nobody can proofread. `kind` names a shape in wardrobe-models.js; a kind that file does not know yet simply does not get drawn, so this file may run ahead of the code.",
